    "frames": [
      {
        "slide": 1,
        "role": "cover",
        "subject": "A tan street_dog mid trot on a straw parkway, warm in the pool against a dark navy chain link fence and a dim limestone house, inside four heavy coral corner marks. A dark A-pillar with a polished bevel runs up the far left edge, and a door sill crosses the bottom under the footer.",
        "visual_consequence": "Without the headline it reads as a loose dog on a night street, seen from inside a car through a detection box, the survey's premise. Bold: median L 4.2, dark 0.813, the dog the brightest form.",
        "weakness": "Only the type changed: the hook sets on three more even lines in the release's tense, clear of the pillar, and the dek ends well above the box. The art is pixel identical to the seventh reading. The raised forepaw is a smooth club and the footer sits on a slightly lighter sill band.",
        "repair": "none required",
        "encoding_reads": true,
        "dominant_subject_finished": true,
