        "slide": 4,
        "role": "evidence",
        "subject": "Two street_dog bodies on one parkway in front of the chain link fence, each fully inside its own coral box. On the left a warm filled mid brown lean dog, head below its withers, ears laid back, ribs showing. On the right a tan dog with a deeper chest, head up, ears pricked, tail raised, stepping forward.",
        "visual_consequence": "Without the labels the two states read as carriage and build, so the release's call by appearance is drawn. The two closed boxes read as two separate detections. Bold: median L 5.1, dark 0.742.",
        "weakness": "Unchanged from the sixth reading. The stray's tucked tail is a dark curve between its hind legs, its laid back ear a flat dark wedge, the tan dog's nose pad large and glossy, and the kerb and road bands under the labels flat noisy slabs.",
